  "body": "### Problem\nFresh bot 6 logs from the S26 run show that the e-mail form appeared and the old code attempted submission only ~22 ms later. The run then stayed on `/member/login/email` for 60 seconds and failed authentication. The user also observed the credentials appear and then disappear without a real visible login transition.\n\n### Changes\n- wait for the React auth form to settle before filling controlled inputs\n- verify both credential fields still contain the configured values after a stability window; re-fill if Vinted rewrites them\n- resolve the submit control from the exact form containing the e-mail/password inputs instead of relying on one global hard-coded button name\n- before every submit attempt, re-check that credentials are still stable\n- attempt submission in a controlled order: form submit button click -> Enter on password -> `HTMLFormElement.requestSubmit()`\n- require an observable post-submit transition; a completed Playwright click alone is no longer treated as success\n- detect and report explicit authentication errors separately\n- improve diagnostics without logging credential values\n- human verification is now reported only from positive evidence (challenge iframe/text); ordinary DOM-read exceptions during navigation no longer count as a CAPTCHA\n- add regression tests for accepted/rejected login submit labels\n\n### Safety\n- no credentials are logged\n- authenticated session is saved only after a real authenticated signal\n- no real marketplace offer/negotiation behavior is changed\n- human-verification handling remains fail-safe when an actual challenge is visible",
